{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler","id":1100429,"title":"How would your character or splat fight a Nexus Crawler?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-05T06:57:24-07:00","id":1100429,"title":"How would your character or splat fight a Nexus Crawler?","content":"So how can you or your group take down a Nexus Crawler? I assume it will involve getting the first strike in and shutting down its ability to channel essence. But has anyone come up with a decent strategy for fighting them, even if it involves mixed parties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T07:15:36-07:00","id":1100436,"title":"","content":"Running away is a really good idea. When you face a Nexus Crawler, remember the old saying 'I do not have to run faster than it, I have than you'. That is one of the reasons why Fera survive better against Nexus Crawlers than most other splats, they can turn into animals and outrun any human. Every other splat requires special abilities to run away fast enough.<br /> <br /> Nexus Crawlers are just impossible to balance because they can do anything. They can also just leave if the fight turns against them, since most splats cannot follow them into the Umbra (and most Fera would count it as a win condition if they drove off a Nexus Crawler).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T09:18:23-07:00","id":1100466,"title":"","content":"But surely there must be some choke hold you can get them in to cut them off from their power. Also, can you define &quot;anything?&quot; Surely not create a Pit or a pristine Glen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T11:19:42-07:00","id":1100515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100466#post1100466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But surely there must be some choke hold you can get them in to cut them off from their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just pictured a werewolf putting a Nexus Crawler in a rear-naked choke.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T12:37:23-07:00","id":1100530,"title":"","content":"I suppose a really powerful Mage with Spirit/Dimensional Science 5 and a similar ranking in Prime could stand a chance of actually defeating one if they have the time to prepare for it. Caught off guard they'd be able to flee from it or possibly drive it away if they're geared up for a fight and get reasonably lucky. I can't really imagine a scenario where one of the other Supernaturals would be able to defeat one using only their own abilities and skill sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T12:41:18-07:00","id":1100532,"title":"","content":"I usually use a Setite character when I'm the player and not the Storyteller.<br /> Therefore, given the request...<br /> 1. if my character knows what's a Nexus Crawler, he would probably harass the nearest Garou pack, making them think his haven is in the &quot;nest&quot; of the Nexus Crawler, then let them deal with the problem, meanwhile leave the city as fast as possible.<br /> 2. otherwise, if there's a problem you can't solve with enough TNT, is only because you didn't used enough...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T13:53:09-07:00","id":1100566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler#post1100429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how can you or your group take down a Nexus Crawler? I assume it will involve getting the first strike in and shutting down its ability to channel essence. But has anyone come up with a decent strategy for fighting them, even if it involves mixed parties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of specific Effects generated with Magick, I don't know that there are any canon ways to &quot;shut down&quot; a Nexus Crawler. And really the Magick angle only works because the Sphere system can literally accomplish anything.<br /> <br /> On point though, show up with enough canon fodder to hopefully distract the Crawler long enough for you to do enough damage to kill it or get it to leave. That's your best bet. With Warp Reality it should be able to escape from pretty much any means of trying to trap it. And they have enough Essence to take a beating if you do manage to harm it. Do your best to stay out of reach of the thing too (might be impossible to do) since even without Charms the creature is pretty deadly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100466#post1100466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But surely there must be some choke hold you can get them in to cut them off from their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. A Spirit's power isn't generally something you can cut it off from, because it's part of what makes the spirit what it is.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T14:05:52-07:00","id":1100574,"title":"","content":"The problem with canon fodder is that Warp Reality can be area effect. A 'Transform Argon to Serin gas' effect could kill everything living with 100 yards. The only real reason why Nexus Crawlers do not bother people more is that they seem to find the material realm rather boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T14:13:18-07:00","id":1100580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100574#post1100574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with canon fodder is that Warp Reality can be area effect. A 'Transform Argon to Serin gas' effect could kill everything living with 100 yards. The only real reason why Nexus Crawlers do not bother people more is that they seem to find the material realm rather boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is entirely fair. By &quot;cannon fodder&quot; I meant at least a dozen legitimate (supernatural) threats. Not random people or Ghoul types. You are going to need opponents for it that can stand up to it physically and mentally and not break immediately. Otherwise the Nexus Crawler has no reason to pay them the least bit of attention, which is the entire point of bringing said fodder along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T14:17:54-07:00","id":1100581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100574#post1100574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not really. A Spirit's power isn't generally something you can cut it off from, because it's part of what makes the spirit what it is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But maybe prevent it from being channeled? In Hunter there was an Edge that allowed you to cut off a super from access to their gnosis, rage, blood, glamour, quint, pathos, and presumably essence. I'm guessing a Mage could do something similar with Prime 3 and maybe Spirit 3 or 4 and beat the super in a contested roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T14:32:14-07:00","id":1100590,"title":"","content":"Are we allowed to use stuff that's in our chronicle? Because there's 3 Chaos Monitors defending a location in our game so.. we'd correspondence and spirit to drop the Nexus Crawler there..<br /> <br /> Chaos Monitors have the &quot;Fuck you reality warper&quot; charm so..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 06-05-2017, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T15:27:32-07:00","id":1100619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100581#post1100581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But maybe prevent it from being channeled? In Hunter there was an Edge that allowed you to cut off a super from access to their gnosis, rage, blood, glamour, quint, pathos, and presumably essence. I'm guessing a Mage could do something similar with Prime 3 and maybe Spirit 3 or 4 and beat the super in a contested roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted the wrong person but: Personally I think that takes too much of a system approach to it. Knowledge of the Essence/Gnosis/Rage/Willpower systems for Spirits are for us the players. Spirits <i>are</i> those stats. They can't be separated from them.<br /> <br /> Approaching from the system side though, the Hunter edge would outright fail since Nexus Crawlers are beyond their power. A Mage could theoretically do it (again since Spheres get to do literally anything), but only really by cheesing the Ritual system to build up enough successes beforehand. The entire Ritual system seems designed to be abused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 06-05-2017, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T16:09:18-07:00","id":1100628,"title":"","content":"The Edge could work. I mean, it depends on the ST, really, Hunters have very &quot;absolute&quot; powers, you &quot;can't&quot; dominate them, &quot;can't&quot; confound them with ilusions. Until you can, of course (like with Elder Disciplines or Mages with Prime 4). In the end the Edge doesn't explicitly states that it blocks the Essence, but it could. Or maybe it only works on lesser spirits.<br /> <br /> With Spirit 4 you can denegate a spirit to use any of it's powers. It's part of the standard &quot;Binding/Warding&quot; stuff. Of course, this it's harder against powerful spirits, so it will be really costly and time consuming...but if you think you *have* to face a Crawler, then it may be time for a variation of the old Taftani &quot;genie in the bottle&quot; trick.<br /> I mention this way to deal with a Crawler not because it would be the most effective, but because it's not a &quot;too much of a system approach to it&quot;. It has history trapping beings with the power of altering reality any way they want, surpassing even the versatility and power of the mages who ensnared them. Of course, those mages were left with a genie they could bargain with when they dared to open the bottle, you're left with a hideous jar full of &quot;chaotic evil&quot; that you will want to dispose with extreme precaution.<br /> <br /> With Correspondence 3 you teleport away, it's cheaper and needs little preparation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A Crawler materializes with &quot;just&quot; 12 Health Levels, so, technically, system wise, isn't impossible for a fearsomely powerful character to win initiative and cause enough damage to send it back to the Umbra before the thing can do anything but being terrifying and madness inducing (something worth to note, as this can send the powerful character screaming in madness).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-05-2017, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T16:29:24-07:00","id":1100638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100628#post1100628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Spirit 4 you can denegate a spirit to use any of it's powers. It's part of the standard &quot;Binding/Warding&quot; stuff. Of course, this it's harder against powerful spirits, so it will be really costly and time consuming...but if you think you *have* to face a Crawler, then it may be time for a variation of the old Taftani &quot;genie in the bottle&quot; trick.<br /> I mention this way to deal with a Crawler not because it would be the most effective, but because it's not a &quot;too much of a system approach to it&quot;. It has history trapping beings with the power of altering reality any way they want, surpassing even the versatility and power of the mages who ensnared them. Of course, those mages were left with a genie they could bargain with when they dared to open the bottle, you're left with a hideous jar full of &quot;chaotic evil&quot; that you will want to dispose with extreme precaution.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I bind them into red and white balls!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T19:03:13-07:00","id":1100676,"title":"","content":"Chaos Monitors might not fare too well against a crawler, even with 3 on 1. Crawlers can get up to a 100 Essence, while Chaos Monitors are generally stuck at a paltry 26 points. As are Stasis Vectors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100436#post1100436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running away is a really good idea</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, it's something that you might do anyway, since their manifesting form is typically hideous and terrible enough to induce Delirium in humans and make some kind of unique roll to resist fox frenzy in Garou and Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T20:17:50-07:00","id":1100684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100676#post1100676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chaos Monitors might not fare too well against a crawler, even with 3 on 1. Crawlers can get up to a 100 Essence, while Chaos Monitors are generally stuck at a paltry 26 points. As are Stasis Vectors.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The ones in book of the Weaver have 60","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T20:57:37-07:00","id":1100691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100684#post1100684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ones in book of the Weaver have 60</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they have a <i>Power</i> of 60, a Trait that ceased to be around Revised. Technically, NCs also got a lower Essence in Revised, but W20 bumped it back up to a high number so that they would be more threatening than most Weaver-spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T21:54:11-07:00","id":1100707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100691#post1100691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they have a <i>Power</i> of 60, a Trait that ceased to be around Revised. Technically, NCs also got a lower Essence in Revised, but W20 bumped it back up to a high number so that they would be more threatening than most Weaver-spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The St has definately been playing these very different.. including giving stasis to them. I Still think Stasis is the key to messing with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T22:16:30-07:00","id":1100713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100628#post1100628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Crawler materializes with &quot;just&quot; 12 Health Levels, so, technically, system wise, isn't impossible for a fearsomely powerful character to win initiative and cause enough damage to send it back to the Umbra before the thing can do anything but being terrifying and madness inducing (something worth to note, as this can send the powerful character screaming in madness).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. It's not &quot;just&quot; 12 Health Levels. Technically it can have any many HL as it's willing to pay for at the time of Materialization. Either way though, it's much more likely to have to fight a NC in the Umbra. They have little reason to pay the cost of crossing over generally speaking.<br /> <br /> And I agree with the point of view presented for using Mage along to do it. But there is the odd bit about Spirit power levels mattering for how difficult the Magick is going to be. And Nexus Crawlers are pretty high up there in power level in general. But yea, Mages can do anything with Ritual Magick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100707#post1100707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The St has definately been playing these very different.. including giving stasis to them. I Still think Stasis is the key to messing with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Chaos Monitors are described as the Weaver's &quot;shock troops&quot; I would not bet on them against a Nexus Crawler. They're rough Wyrm equivalent would be Scrags. The 2 Charms they have that seem of use (Spirit Static and Solidify Reality) both fail to stack up against Warp Reality. Solidify might be able to protect an object at a time (a fairly big maybe) and Static Reality just raises the Gauntlet. Neither protect against what Warp Reality does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T22:46:57-07:00","id":1100720,"title":"","content":"In theory I suppose Spirit Manipulation 4 could work on a Nexus Crawler if one could find an appropriate vessel, but I wouldn't want to bet on that happening. And even if it worked you wouldn't want something with that much bad juju sticking around anywhere that people could stumble across it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T23:24:43-07:00","id":1100727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100713#post1100713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. It's not &quot;just&quot; 12 Health Levels. Technically it can have any many HL as it's willing to pay for at the time of Materialization.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not how it works from Revised onward. It just poofs out on the other end of the gauntlet if the gauntlet is equal to or lower than its Gnosis. It uses its spirit stats in place of everything, without the need to pay even one point of Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T01:29:55-07:00","id":1100753,"title":"","content":"1. Entropy 5, intellectual entropy, swap the meaning of winning and retreating/or just link the concept of retreat with the concept of winning.<br /> <br /> 2. Retreat<br /> <br /> 3. Since retreat is winning...you just won.<br /> <br /> Another cheesy way would be the Immunity merit out of Guide to the Traditions.<br /> If you invest 10+ points you are nigh impossible to kill.<br /> Recommended to take precautions against horrible mind shattering things the NC could do to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T06:18:41-07:00","id":1100797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100713#post1100713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Considering that Chaos Monitors are described as the Weaver's &quot;shock troops&quot; I would not bet on them against a Nexus Crawler. They're rough Wyrm equivalent would be Scrags. The 2 Charms they have that seem of use (Spirit Static and Solidify Reality) both fail to stack up against Warp Reality. Solidify might be able to protect an object at a time (a fairly big maybe) and Static Reality just raises the Gauntlet. Neither protect against what Warp Reality does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I saw the canon of them, which is vastly different than how the ST has been portraying them. Which is his right and its fun so my view was kind of off. I thought they had the charm Stasis which basically turns off powers or makes them hard to use. In the same vein I Suggest a Devil Tiger with a swarm of Bakemono each with homogeneity, spam it while the Devil Tiger uses Blood Awakening on the Nexus crawler. All the KJ needs is one hit and the Nexus Crawler is completely and utterly frozen unable to act whatsoever.<br /> <br /> So spit on Nexus Crawler. and Cast Either Asserting the Heavenly Privlege of Yang Demon Command or Greater Inauspicious item and gain that precious point of Dharma you so deserve...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T07:04:09-07:00","id":1100814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100727#post1100727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's not how it works from Revised onward. It just poofs out on the other end of the gauntlet if the gauntlet is equal to or lower than its Gnosis. It uses its spirit stats in place of everything, without the need to pay even one point of Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah okay, I see what you mean by that. A flat 12 Health Levels seems a bit silly. Fair enough though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100797#post1100797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah I saw the canon of them, which is vastly different than how the ST has been portraying them. Which is his right and its fun so my view was kind of off.</div> </div> </div> </div>That happens. Fun is more important than systems, but can lead to issues is discussion on the forums when you misremember something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100797#post1100797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the same vein I Suggest a Devil Tiger with a swarm of Bakemono each with homogeneity, spam it while the Devil Tiger uses Blood Awakening on the Nexus crawler. All the KJ needs is one hit and the Nexus Crawler is completely and utterly frozen unable to act whatsoever.<br /> <br /> So spit on Nexus Crawler. and Cast Either Asserting the Heavenly Privlege of Yang Demon Command or Greater Inauspicious item and gain that precious point of Dharma you so deserve...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Homogeneity would work on a Nexus Crawler. Nor should it be 1 shotted by any particular power. The concept of a &quot;helpless&quot; (the word used under Blood Awakening) NC is just kind of bizarre.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T07:20:56-07:00","id":1100820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100814#post1100814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Homogeneity would work on a Nexus Crawler. Nor should it be 1 shotted by any particular power. The concept of a &quot;helpless&quot; (the word used under Blood Awakening) NC is just kind of bizarre.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wyrm turns against itself is a pretty solid theme. The premise of the DT Dharma is using wickedness to bring evil spirits back in line(among others). And while I agree one shotting with even a level 5 discipline is kind of odd(and that power is particularly poorly written out, which is impressive to say the least), I'd probably move it to the NC requires 1 application of the discipline for every 10 essence they have rounded up.. so between 3 for a small and 12 for a larger. It still gets an impressive dodge option and can always close your face after taht first spit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T08:09:22-07:00","id":1100845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100814#post1100814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah okay, I see what you mean by that. A flat 12 Health Levels seems a bit silly. Fair enough though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's part of the greater Nostalgia Edition nature of W20 as opposed to, say, C20, or presumably Wr20. A lot of stuff just got kept on because, like that one Charm a Dream Maker bane has that has no mechanical definition, and never has, as opposed to every system in Changeling getting completely overhauled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T08:10:39-07:00","id":1100846,"title":"","content":"Homogenity is much less of an 'I shut you down' power in W20. The Fomori spend one point of Willpower and rolls a contested Manipulation plus Intimidation (difficulty 7) against the target's Willpower (difficulty 6). With each net success, the Fomori removes one die from the die pool to activate the next power used by the target. At best, a bunch of Fomori could prevent a Nexus Crawler from using Warp Reality for a turn. <br /> <br /> Nexus Crawlers are dangerous because of their unpredictability, not just because of their raw power, but they can be overwhelmed with sufficient numbers. The problem is that they can appear anywhere, at anytime, due to their Gnosis 10, so they can attack you when you are not prepared for them and they most likely will. A Nexus Crawler will rarely be so accommodating as to randomly Materialize into existence in the middle of an army of bakemono. They are phenomenally intelligence (they use their Gnosis 10 for their Mental Dice Pools), so they should use highly effective strategy and tactics (even if they do not seem to follow any discernible logic to the Garou). In addition, they can cause Delirium in most bakemono unless the bakemono is specifically immune to Delirium (and are still horrific enough to force the bakemono to make a Willpower roll to avoid running gibbering away even if they are immune to Delirium).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T09:28:57-07:00","id":1100862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100753#post1100753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another cheesy way would be the Immunity merit out of Guide to the Traditions.<br /> If you invest 10+ points you are nigh impossible to kill.<br /> Recommended to take precautions against horrible mind shattering things the NC could do to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this image of such a Mage somehow being able to ride a Nexus Crawler around the Umbra, and in battles...kind of like Sandworm-riding in <i>Dune</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T11:21:34-07:00","id":1100891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">they should use highly effective strategy and tactics (even if they do not seem to follow any discernible logic to the Garou)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was stated somewhere that if this was the case the Garou Nation would be no more (I think it was in Revised rp of the thing). Maybe the tactics are effective, but they don't care to &quot;win battles&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Homogenity is much less of an 'I shut you down' power in W20. The Fomori spend one point of Willpower and rolls a contested Manipulation plus Intimidation (difficulty 7) against the target's Willpower (difficulty 6). With each net success, the Fomori removes one die from the die pool to activate the next power used by the target. At best, a bunch of Fomori could prevent a Nexus Crawler from using Warp Reality for a turn. </div> </div> </div>Well, the Crawler has six dice, and is my understanding that it can't do much with less that three net successes vs dif. 7, so this tactic may be good. Reduce it to 2 or less dice each turn and the Crawler would be limmited to things at the level of blurry ilusions and minor alterations to the temperature. Of course, it's still a slavering monster with Strenght 10 and up to 100 hp, so it's not likely it's defeated, but it's a good start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T11:47:30-07:00","id":1100899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100891#post1100891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Crawler has six dice, and is my understanding that it can't do much with less that three net successes vs dif. 7, so this tactic may be good. Reduce it to 2 or less dice each turn and the Crawler would be limmited to things at the level of blurry ilusions and minor alterations to the temperature. Of course, it's still a slavering monster with Strenght 10 and up to 100 hp, so it's not likely it's defeated, but it's a good start.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be, but Homogenity is supposed to cancel Supernatural powers. Not innate Supernatural abilities, which is where I feel Spirit Charms fall under. For example Homogenity can cancel Gifts, but not a Garou's ability to shapeshift. Spirits are not supposed to have learned powers as such.This is obviously just my take on it though (and I can see the argument against). <br /> <br /> I personally don't think this particular power should have any effect on spirits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T11:48:54-07:00","id":1100900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100846#post1100846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homogenity is much less of an 'I shut you down' power in W20. The Fomori spend one point of Willpower and rolls a contested Manipulation plus Intimidation (difficulty 7) against the target's Willpower (difficulty 6). With each net success, the Fomori removes one die from the die pool to activate the next power used by the target. At best, a bunch of Fomori could prevent a Nexus Crawler from using Warp Reality for a turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the point. Make warp reality harder to use for afew turns while you freeze the NC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nexus Crawlers are dangerous because of their unpredictability, not just because of their raw power, but they can be overwhelmed with sufficient numbers. The problem is that they can appear anywhere, at anytime, due to their Gnosis 10, so they can attack you when you are not prepared for them and they most likely will. A Nexus Crawler will rarely be so accommodating as to randomly Materialize into existence in the middle of an army of bakemono. They are phenomenally intelligence (they use their Gnosis 10 for their Mental Dice Pools), so they should use highly effective strategy and tactics (even if they do not seem to follow any discernible logic to the Garou). In addition, they can cause Delirium in most bakemono unless the bakemono is specifically immune to Delirium (and are still horrific enough to force the bakemono to make a Willpower roll to avoid running gibbering away even if they are immune to Delirium). </div> </div> </div>While a Nexus crawler might randomly jump you in the middle of the city they are more likely to make important attacks. A Caern/Dragon's nest for example. I'm assuming its making an attack in a valuable target which would have a level of defense. <br /> <br /> The &quot;it will strike when you can't use your best powers&quot; seems serious goal post shifting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T11:55:31-07:00","id":1100905,"title":"","content":"How many bakemono can you support as a DT? Can you support large numbers 24-7? What about the other splats? I doubt that many Fera want to waste Kinfolk on keeping a NC distracted and I doubt that many Kindred know enough about them to make effective plans for Ghoul deployment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T16:02:55-07:00","id":1100998,"title":"","content":"@Aya Tari: Mechanic check: Devil-Tiger demonologists could, in 2e, bind a number of banes with a summed Power equal to or less than 20 x (P'o + Occult), and going above half that is a giant strain. If you're assuming the equivalent of about 40 power to make a combat-worthy bakemono, you could reasonably expect about 3 to 5 for younger Devil-Tigers, and up to about 9 or 10 for elders. If the younger vampire is dangerously unhinged, however, the number could be on par with a nelder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100900#post1100900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be the point. Make warp reality harder to use for afew turns while you freeze the NC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in mind that it's usually warping reality while it's simultaneously ripping into you with its Rage of 10.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While a Nexus crawler might randomly jump you in the middle of the city they are more likely to make important attacks. A Caern/Dragon's nest for example. I'm assuming its making an attack in a valuable target which would have a level of defense.<br /> <br /> The &quot;it will strike when you can't use your best powers&quot; seems serious goal post shifting to me. </div> </div> </div>It strikes in the same equivalent conditions where a tornado, earthquake, or wildfire would. Such is its nature as much more of a force than a person.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T17:52:25-07:00","id":1101044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100998#post1100998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Aya Tari: Mechanic check: Devil-Tiger demonologists could, in 2e, bind a number of banes with a summed Power equal to or less than 20 x (P'o + Occult), and going above half that is a giant strain. If you're assuming the equivalent of about 40 power to make a combat-worthy bakemono, you could reasonably expect about 3 to 5 for younger Devil-Tigers, and up to about 9 or 10 for elders. If the younger vampire is dangerously unhinged, however, the number could be on par with a nelder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bakemono Rite says if you use a bound bane it keeps it forever it doesn't quite count anymore plus they can make them with nonbound banes..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keeping in mind that it's usually warping reality while it's simultaneously ripping into you with its Rage of 10. </div> </div> </div>That's what the army is for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It strikes in the same equivalent conditions where a tornado, earthquake, or wildfire would. Such is its nature as much more of a force than a person.<br /> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem to be the case? I mean they broadly seem to match &quot;Veil/masquerade/etc&quot; setup so less drop in the middle of a city. Though there are good chances of getting hit alone.. and Dumb Devil Tigers can summon them.<br /> <br /> But I think its fair to have &quot;how would you fight them if you are prepared&quot; vs &quot;How to handle a Nexus crawler if you are naked in a white room&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T18:55:09-07:00","id":1101069,"title":"","content":"How can you prepare for a Nexus Crawler? They do not obey rules of engagement and operate by inhuman logic. They are just as likely to ambush you while you are eating Chinese as they are to jump you while you are on the john. In fact, they are less likely to attack you at a Caern because a Caern has guardians beyond the Garou. Nexus Crawlers are the definition of an unfair fight because they can come at your character from any direction, at any time, without regards to your level of preparation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T00:45:18-07:00","id":1101138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1101069#post1101069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can you prepare for a Nexus Crawler? They do not obey rules of engagement and operate by inhuman logic. They are just as likely to ambush you while you are eating Chinese as they are to jump you while you are on the john. In fact, they are less likely to attack you at a Caern because a Caern has guardians beyond the Garou. Nexus Crawlers are the definition of an unfair fight because they can come at your character from any direction, at any time, without regards to your level of preparation.</div> </div> </div> </div>A paranoid mage could send massive amounts of rituals into a (possible) future.<br /> <br /> Or predict when and where a NC attacks.<br /> <br /> Or makes sure to make only telepresence visits outside of the sanctum.<br /> <br /> Or...<br /> <br /> As has been said, spheres can theoretically do anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T08:16:39-07:00","id":1101228,"title":"","content":"A Baali could <i>bind</i> a Nexus Crawler, what with the Baali's dominion over that sort of entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T10:09:24-07:00","id":1101277,"title":"","content":"Or just summon some other cosmic horrors to fight it and then wander off to find a snack. <br /> <br /> An earthbound could just sue it for intellectual property infringement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T12:09:59-07:00","id":1101323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1101228#post1101228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Baali could <i>bind</i> a Nexus Crawler, what with the Baali's dominion over that sort of entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would probably depend on how literally the Storyteller interprets the word &quot;demon&quot; in the write-ups for Dark Thaumaturgy and the Kraina of the Well. Some might regard it as a potato/pot<i>ah</i>to type deal, others might insist on the powers only working on the Fallen, or spirits from high umbral hells, or minions of whatever particular dread masters the Baali serve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T12:12:33-07:00","id":1101327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1101228#post1101228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Baali could <i>bind</i> a Nexus Crawler, what with the Baali's dominion over that sort of entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? I do not think that Nexus Crawlers count as demons according to the definitions of the Baali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T12:20:16-07:00","id":1101331,"title":"","content":"What defines a 'demon' in context of the Baali depends on what gameline and source material you read; i.e. in Book of Madness, the Nephandi count the Baali as an offshoot of their own forebears, and so would place the forces they wield in line with the horrors that the Nephandi worship, including the Wyrm and thus Nexus Crawlers. The 'Children' by a straight reading also resemble the Neverborn, who are tied to (are the origin of or source of the corruption of) the Wyrm in Mage etc.; a general argument could be made that the Wyrm/Neverborn/Abyss are all just levels of Oblivion's corruption/destructive urge, and that the stuff that the Baali and their forebears wielded all tied into that. I'd probably allow relevant Daimoinon powers to manipulate Banes and the like, but to compel a Nexus Crawler you'd need a massive dice pool and an enormous number of successes.<br /> <br /> The interpretation of the Baali as tied to the Earthbound/fallen really only comes from Devil's Due.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T13:03:48-07:00","id":1101348,"title":"","content":"'Denom' really just means 'evil spirit', as far as I see things. This includes D:tF demons, M:tAs Astral Umbral demons and gribbly Outsider Things that exist at the very point where space/time comes to a stop, W:tA Banes and W:tO Spectres, among other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T14:08:47-07:00","id":1101363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1101228#post1101228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Baali could <i>bind</i> a Nexus Crawler, what with the Baali's dominion over that sort of entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>With which power? I'm not being argumentative, but the wording of the specific power really will matter.<br /> <br /> Though I do not agree that any &quot;evil spirit&quot; counts the same as a &quot;demon&quot; within the WoD in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T15:39:51-07:00","id":1101395,"title":"","content":"Daimoinon 7 only refers to the summoning of Celestial beings of evil (High Umbra spirits in WtA and MtAs and Demons in DtF). It is also a 7th level power, so you would be facing a 6th generation Baali, which should have better ways of killing you than an entity that is only controlled for a short time and cannot be banished, only killed with difficulty. It also creates a generic body for the spirit rather than summoning the spirit into the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 06-07-2017, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T15:50:15-07:00","id":1101396,"title":"","content":"I wasn't just referring to Daimoinon, but also Dark Thaumaturgy---a Discipline Baali frequently learn from the horrible entities that rule over them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T17:09:40-07:00","id":1101413,"title":"","content":"And what Path do you propose to use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T18:09:30-07:00","id":1101434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1101413#post1101413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what Path do you propose to use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a clue. I'm not well-versed in Dark Thaumaturgy Paths and rituals, so, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T19:49:10-07:00","id":1101470,"title":"","content":"Really? Where does it mention that the Baali get Dark Thaumaturgy (or any Thaumaturgy) in V20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T22:28:26-07:00","id":1101498,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgy is in general fairly specific about the entities it deals with. That's why you end up with so many Wards. And Ward against Demons does not work against spirits. Without a specific power being cited, I can only assume that &quot;demon&quot; in this context will not encompass Nexus Crawlers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:18:36-07:00","id":1101577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1101470#post1101470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Where does it mention that the Baali get Dark Thaumaturgy (or any Thaumaturgy) in V20?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say <i>any</i> infernalist gets Dark Thaumaturgy? Demons teach it to their slaves. It's not an in-clan Disciple, but, if, as a Kindred, you sell your soul, learning the rudiments of it are easily explained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:35:15-07:00","id":1101583,"title":"","content":"But Baali are not Infernalists, they serve the Children, not the Demon Lords, so they do not gain the benefits of being an Infernalist. It specifically says in V20 (p. 394) that they are a nihilistic Bloodline that refuses to make Faustian bargains because they believe that such bargains are futile. It would be against the teaching of the Baali to engage in Dark Thaumaturgy or other forms of Soul Commerce because of their nihilistic attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T04:18:30-07:00","id":1101915,"title":"","content":"Nexus Crawlers are often used in scenes where there are more then just your pack fighting it. I've say used one in a prologue story representing a big sept battle against a hive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T13:49:24-07:00","id":1102097,"title":"","content":"Earlier in this thread someone mentioned the fact that the thing only has 12 HL when materialized, which I find incredibly important to this discussion--you necessarily want to fight a NC in the real world in light of this fact, cause in the Umbra (basically) <i>at least </i>twice as hearty--and even if we split the baby between the min and and max, that's till 65 essence, which basically means you're going to stand there and whack away at the thing (probably) for a while as it takes often illogical or absurd potshots at your with Warp Reality.<br /> <br /> I actually threw a NC against my group last weekend. The group is made up of 4 mages: one VA, one SoE, one Akashik, and one Hermetic. We've been playing a few years, so everyone has one or two spheres at 4, three our four spheres at 2-3, and between one to three spheres at 1. You know, no slouches. I made the mistake of having the NC materialize, rolled okay init for the NC; three of the four other mages did really well and beat the NC's init, and they basically dismantled the thing before it could get a shot off. It has neither the Armor charm, nor any way of taking extra actions--so even using a House rule we have that allows for a single reflexive dodge using only Dex (and I allowed the NC to use it's full WP, mind)--they got to 12 health levels <u><i>real quick</i></u>.<br /> <br /> But then, as I said, I made the mistake of having the thing materialize rather than simply contrive of a way for them to fight it in the umbra. Live and learn, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T19:52:51-07:00","id":1102176,"title":"","content":"Rocket launchers enhanced with Prime works always. Uhh, also sending in 40 Hit Marks; you can buy a lot of Hit Marks with 15 freebie points. Hand grenades work equally well. Any guy with about 1000m of clean line of sight and a sniper rifle. A pack of angry werewolves that do only attacks first round of combat can drop it sometimes. Any Cabal with a designated countermagick guy/True Faith guy can wreck them. Actually True Faith in general works.<br /> <br /> And when in doubt, direct a nearby Marauder at it, roll up the scrying mirror and make some popcorn to watch one of the greatest shows on Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T20:10:22-07:00","id":1102177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1102176#post1102176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rocket launchers enhanced with Prime works always. Uhh, also sending in 40 Hit Marks; you can buy a lot of Hit Marks with 15 freebie points. Hand grenades work equally well. Any guy with about 1000m of clean line of sight and a sniper rifle. A pack of angry werewolves that do only attacks first round of combat can drop it sometimes. Any Cabal with a designated countermagick guy/True Faith guy can wreck them. Actually True Faith in general works.<br /> <br /> And when in doubt, direct a nearby Marauder at it, roll up the scrying mirror and make some popcorn to watch one of the greatest shows on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of those don't work unless you have an incredibly low opinion of what Nexus Crawlers are/do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T21:32:23-07:00","id":1102187,"title":"","content":"The simple fact of the matter is that NC have extreme versatility. They can attack you from anywhere, at anytime, because they effectively ignore the Gauntlet with their Gnosis 10. Since their Willpower 6 functions as Dexterity and their Gnosis 10 functions as Wits, they have Initiative 16, which means they will be going before most combat builds (and that is after they had surprise round to attack you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T12:45:03-07:00","id":1102331,"title":"","content":"Primium sniper fire from enhanced rifles might be worth a try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T14:34:28-07:00","id":1102360,"title":"","content":"Yes, assuming that you can be prepared for a NC attack. Prepared positions assume that you are defending a static position or have intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T14:59:17-07:00","id":1102366,"title":"","content":"Well if you can't tell from my Avatar I have played in a more that one Technocracy Game and I was a MiB. So who am I going to call for back up? Well some people call them the Void Engineers but others <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m9We2XsVZfc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m9We2XsVZfc</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T17:12:12-07:00","id":1102396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1102177#post1102177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of those don't work unless you have an incredibly low opinion of what Nexus Crawlers are/do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you have an incredibly over zealous belief in how they work. They require an action to do anything with their rape reality power, countermagick screws that over fast. They only have 12 health levels when materialized too. If you're fighting them in the Umbra, that's another issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T20:55:21-07:00","id":1102428,"title":"","content":"Well, they also tend to go first in combat and hit like a Mach truck, though I agree that they are worst in the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T06:25:11-07:00","id":1102490,"title":"","content":"A D:TF malefactor should be able to create chains or something similar that can drain it's essence to weaken it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T09:43:39-07:00","id":1102540,"title":"","content":"A bit of brainstorming on the Mage side:<br /> <br /> Attacking its Essence may be necessary if battling in the Umbra, but generally a bad Idea. Because they have a ton of Essence (up to 100). In order to blow it up in one shot for sure, a mage would need somewhat like 52 Successes devoted to Damage (assuming maximum Essence). That's not very doable.<br /> An Archmaster of Forces can get that done in 26 successes, more realist, but not easy.<br /> With extra powerful powers like Antimater (that it's successes x3 to damage instead of x2), or those combinations of Prime + Forces that somehow add a multiplier it could be slightly easier, but still hard.<br /> All in all, an Archmaster <i>could </i>have something under his sleeve that does that kind of damage, but it's not as cheap as just eleporting away. Of course, a starship armed to the teeth can dish that kind of damage by deploying misiles and rays, but again, starships ain't exactly cheap.<br /> <br /> NC on the lower ends of the Essence pool are more easy to kill. A normal mage would need 15-17 successes, wich it's reasonable to have under the sleeve. It's still more expensive than runing away.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the thing Materializes with 12 hp or so, it's much more vulnerable to damage attacks, but depending on rules this may not be the case. <hr /><br /> Another approach it's to have something that can reduce it's capability to cause mayheim.<br /> <br /> Countermagic could work because a Crawler's magic depends on having many successes with not that many dice but, since the crawler can do anything, you would need ALL the Spheres to be sure.<br /> Depending on the ST, you may need to use Sphere vs Sphere when countering, meaning having all Spheres at the correct levels to create a similar effect-in that case, the mages would be hard pressed to compete even assuming that they have the dice.<br /> And then, even if you manage it, you still are facing a slavering monster that can overpower werewolves even without using magic.<br /> <br /> While Traditionalist Mages usually flee from scene when faced with such odds, if they stay to fight it's likely to be because they're defending an area. And that means Wards. Now, a NC can probably dispel wards, but not all wards are equal or obvious:<br /> <br /> A Spirit 4 Ward can impede a spirit to Materialize or use any power from the other side of the Ward, but let's say the reality breaking powers of the Crawler allow it to breach the Ward and Materializes or whatever.<br /> You could have built your wards in such a way that when the NC approaches (or breaches your Spirit 4 Ward to Materialize) a big ward activates in the area. But this time it's a Minor Ward (Spirit 2/Prime 2/Corr 2). Minor Wards don't prevent passage, but instead they limmit the hability to act of the baned beings. A Minor Ward substracts dice from ALL the actions of the baned creatures inside the area of effect. With &quot;just&quot; 4-6 dice less at everything, the NC would be unable to use it's powers to breach the Ward nor to break any reality. Bonus points because while you're still facing a slavering monster, the monster now has less dice at everything.<br /> <br /> Much better than Countermagic, if you ask me...and the better part it's that you don't need to win Initiative against the Crawler, nor to expect it. It could work against any Bane that decided to enter (albeit you <i>could </i>make one especific for NC).<br /> <br /> Similar effects could be achieved with Spirit 4 by creating interference in the spiritual power, similarly as when you affect a Werewolf to give her a +3 to all Gifts difficulties. Since NC has to roll to Break Reality, this could be effective. <hr />Yet another approach would be to sidestep the Essence of the beast entirely.<br /> <br /> It's said that Hermetics have a special Time 4 + Correspondence 4 Rote for beings that are too powerful to be defeated. The Rote (probably a ritual chaneled trough an Artifact or a Time trigger) puts the thing outside time and space, efectively removing it from the game until the spell expires. Correspondence vanishes the thing, but Time it's what makes it unable to use it's powers to get free (by freezing the enemy in one second)<br /> <br /> With Time 5, a mage can always stop time and search for enough dinamite to stop it. As has been said, if enough dinamite doesn't work it's because you didn't used enough dinamite.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's the Lord of all Cheese. The &quot;I teleport it somewhere dangerous, like to the Sun&quot;. These things are why people give their creratures Countermagic when Mages enter the table. Still, I would think that such a spell it's unlikely to work without a ritual. <hr />Of these powers that need to be prepared beforehand. The Ward and the Hermetic Seal are the ones that I can see mages may have prepared. The first because no one wants Banes in their yards, and the second because it's a clasic.<br /> Powerful damage rituals ported in charms/gadgets wouldn't be rare either, probably not so powerful as to one shot a potent NC, but still useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-11-2017, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T09:56:21-07:00","id":1102543,"title":"","content":"Another one: With Spirit 5 you can affect the NC spiritual attributes. Lower Willpower to 1-2, and there's no more reality warping. This may be the cheapest way to prevent the being from using powers, rules wise (you usually need 1 successes per At point changed, Countermagic may get in the way if that rule is used). Of course, you're still facing a slavering beast that eats Werewolves for breakfast, so it's not like you won, but if you happen to have an army or a werewolf pack by your side, it could be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T10:06:40-07:00","id":1102546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1102543#post1102543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This may be the cheapest way to prevent the being from using powers, rules wise (you usually need 1 successes per At point changed, Countermagic may get in the way if that rule is used).</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it harder to effect spirits like the Nexus Crawler? Like two, three or even four-five successes needed per point of Willpower lowered.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T18:08:54-07:00","id":1102667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1102543#post1102543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one: With Spirit 5 you can affect the NC spiritual attributes. Lower Willpower to 1-2, and there's no more reality warping. This may be the cheapest way to prevent the being from using powers, rules wise (you usually need 1 successes per At point changed, Countermagic may get in the way if that rule is used). Of course, you're still facing a slavering beast that eats Werewolves for breakfast, so it's not like you won, but if you happen to have an army or a werewolf pack by your side, it could be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding Usul's question. How many successes to you actually need to pull things like that off? Is there some obscure rule about Essence or Power ratings factoring in somewhere in Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T20:30:17-07:00","id":1102694,"title":"","content":"Not that it even matters (for Mage players in particular) but I also feel like this is taking a very heavily system-minded approach to it. Characters don't have access to the system knowledge of how NC's (or any spirit really) does what they do. How or why does the character know to move around a few points of Willpower to cancel out the Reality Warping ability?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T21:16:20-07:00","id":1102702,"title":"","content":"I can see trying something similar with Gnosis on the general principle of removing the spirit's ability to act across the Gauntlet or materialize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T21:35:13-07:00","id":1102704,"title":"","content":"I think that it ignores the horror aspect of the NC to have them come after a PC when she is prepared. If the PC is not vulnerable, the NC should go after the parts of the PC's life that is vulnerable. Of course, this applies to any enemy in a horror setting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T23:26:14-07:00","id":1102716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1102694#post1102694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that it even matters (for Mage players in particular) but I also feel like this is taking a very heavily system-minded approach to it. Characters don't have access to the system knowledge of how NC's (or any spirit really) does what they do. How or why does the character know to move around a few points of Willpower to cancel out the Reality Warping ability?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit sight/sense, and maybe Prime sight/sense, could be used. Entropy 1 could pinpoint it. Perhaps Spirit 1, Time 2, Entropy 1 to show the greatest danger and how to counter it.<br /> I'd say that a character with Spirit 5 should have a good feeling/hunch in regards how to do this. I can imagine that they might even get an automatic Spirit Time divination that warns them of the reality warping (and they would have to roll Arete and/or Willpower to avoid being overwhelmed); Prime and/or Correspondence could make them aware that the Tapestry is close to being changed.<br /> And they wouldn't necessarily see countering the Reality Warp as draining the Willpower of the Nexus Crawler - they might craft a temporary spell that makes the Nexus Crawler's Willpower effectively lower for the purpose of the Reality Warp.<br /> Or they could create a bubble that makes them immune to effects of the warping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-12-2017, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T05:07:46-07:00","id":1102764,"title":"","content":"Reality Warping should probably be considered equivalent to True Magic in capabilities, though it is much more effective than True Magic because it does not suffer from Paradox, its effects are permanent, and witnesses do not weaken its capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T07:11:21-07:00","id":1102795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that it even matters (for Mage players in particular) but I also feel like this is taking a very heavily system-minded approach to it. Characters don't have access to the system knowledge of how NC's (or any spirit really) does what they do. How or why does the character know to move around a few points of Willpower to cancel out the Reality Warping ability?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit sight/sense, and maybe Prime sight/sense, could be used. Entropy 1 could pinpoint it. Perhaps Spirit 1, Time 2, Entropy 1 to show the greatest danger and how to counter it.<br /> I'd say that a character with Spirit 5 should have a good feeling/hunch in regards how to do this. I can imagine that they might even get an automatic Spirit Time divination that warns them of the reality warping (and they would have to roll Arete and/or Willpower to avoid being overwhelmed); Prime and/or Correspondence could make them aware that the Tapestry is close to being changed.<br /> And they wouldn't necessarily see countering the Reality Warp as draining the Willpower of the Nexus Crawler - they might craft a temporary spell that makes the Nexus Crawler's Willpower effectively lower for the purpose of the Reality Warp.<br /> Or they could create a bubble that makes them immune to effects of the warping.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this it's true, it's true that such an approach would need a ton of Lore, in spite of the fact that a powerful Spirit Master may have a fairly good share of lore and ways to attain it. The posibility exists, but that doesn't mean your average Mage can take advantage of it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconding Usul's question. How many successes to you actually need to pull things like that off? Is there some obscure rule about Essence or Power ratings factoring in somewhere in Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, the Spirit 5 effect would sidestep Essence. If you're going to face the spirit Essence then it's better to Bind it (or put it in a bottle, like I suggested earlier), if you manage to do it then the Spirit it's effectively neutralized and you've WON.<br /> The Spirit 5 approach doesn't get you an instant win (the spirit still has two other attributes and can easily destroy a weak human with it's Rage), but saves you the pain of facing 30 to 100 points of Essence, thus <i>potentially </i>making the feat much cheaper than it would be otherwise, even if it isn't the most common or realistic way to do it.<br /> There's no rules about number of successes. Usually, when you affect Traits, it's one success per point of Trait lowered or increased(+ 2 on Duration to make it last a scene, if playing with Revised), though if the ST feels that Master magick affecting NC undermines the awesomeness that these creatures should have it's entitled to make it cost more, but there's no rule that says affecting powerful spirits with this it's harder than affecting weak ones (Paradox spirits have special rules vs magick, the rest haven't that advantage), so you should determine the number of successes to affect all spirits, among other things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it ignores the horror aspect of the NC to have them come after a PC when she is prepared. If the PC is not vulnerable, the NC should go after the parts of the PC's life that is vulnerable. Of course, this applies to any enemy in a horror setting...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the beauty of Wards, you put them in places that you care for, where you would rather stand and fight instead of fleeing. If Banes don't appear at all because of that, much better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reality Warping should probably be considered equivalent to True Magic in capabilities, though it is much more effective than True Magic because it does not suffer from Paradox, its effects are permanent, and witnesses do not weaken its capabilities. </div> </div> </div>In Mage, powerful spirits are given Spheres and Arete to represent this kind of power. So, yeah, totally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-12-2017, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T07:27:03-07:00","id":1102801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1102704#post1102704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it ignores the horror aspect of the NC to have them come after a PC when she is prepared. If the PC is not vulnerable, the NC should go after the parts of the PC's life that is vulnerable. Of course, this applies to any enemy in a horror setting...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can agree with your point I think there's much potential horror in an planned attack on a Nexus Crawler(Or Hive or even Seige) since for all the supposed heroism that might come of these, alot of people are going to die. Alot of people just like you. Its like D-day, for all the planning, for all the things that went perfectly it was a blood bath. So maybe your mages or werewolves or KJ or what have you survive maybe they get the killing blow in. But there will be losses and it will be the most vulnerable. The Cubs, the Kinfolk, the assistants, the spirit allies. Names and faces that you have built up to matter to the players that they will never see again.<br /> <br /> Hammering in their face their ultimate powerlessness even at their most triumphant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T14:03:06-07:00","id":1102909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1102795#post1102795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> All of this it's true, it's true that such an approach would need a ton of Lore, in spite of the fact that a powerful Spirit Master may have a fairly good share of lore and ways to attain it. The posibility exists, but that doesn't mean your average Mage can take advantage of it</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point though, the amount of Lore needed would have to include studies of Nexus Crawlers specifically to know what traits govern what abilities for this specific spirit. I think when you are getting to that level of system mechanics that just isn't available to characters.<br /> Personally I think the spirit system (Rage/Gnosis/Will/Essence) is incredibly simplified for us the players. In character they should seem a lot more complex than that. I don't think it should be possible to reduce all spirits down to that limited system in character. Nevermind that the character is apparently connecting a Spirit's Willpower Rating to their ability to use a specific Charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1102795#post1102795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In Mage, powerful spirits are given Spheres and Arete to represent this kind of power. So, yeah, totally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think maybe it comes down to this. It's more of a game translation issue than anything else. If a NC were to appear in Mage instead of WtA, it should be given Sphere ratings (even if only virtual ones) to cover the concept of what they're supposed to do/be. I'd imagine they would also have a form of innate countermagic, given what they are/represent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T23:25:20-07:00","id":1103025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1102795#post1102795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of this it's true, it's true that such an approach would need a ton of Lore, in spite of the fact that a powerful Spirit Master may have a fairly good share of lore and ways to attain it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1102909#post1102909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point though, the amount of Lore needed would have to include studies of Nexus Crawlers specifically to know what traits govern what abilities for this specific spirit. I think when you are getting to that level of system mechanics that just isn't available to characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that I think Spirit and/or Prime and/or Entropy sight(s) (or sense(s) ) could reveal the connection between the Willpower and the Reality Warp; in whatever way/terms that would make sense to the Mage's Paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T23:57:19-07:00","id":1103030,"title":"","content":"Personally I believe that when a mage witnesses a NC warping reality then he can attempt to weaken that ability.<br /> Whether it is via warding, antimagick or altering the NC directly is not a matter of Lore. It is a matter of spheres.<br /> If it wasn't then you have to have Lore for other feats of magick as well: \u201cSorry but your Life 2 is not sufficient to heal yourself, you are lacking the Lore of the body/healing/whatever.\u201c<br /> <br /> Mage is about changing reality.<br /> To put additional hindrances to the ones already present(Arete, Spheres, successes needed, instruments) makes the game a hassle.<br /> <br /> Important distinction: an attempt means not that there is a success. But if a mage has the relevant spheres he gets a shot at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T05:28:34-07:00","id":1103089,"title":"","content":"I think that in Mage terms, NC would effectively have Arete 6 with Forces 6, Life 6, Matter 6, Prime 6, and Spirit 6 (and a pool of Quintessence equal to their Essence). I think that would be the easiest conversion of Warp Reality to the Mage system, as Warp Reality can do things that even Masters have difficulty imagining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T06:52:52-07:00","id":1103114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I think that in Mage terms, NC would effectively have Arete 6 with Forces 6, Life 6, Matter 6, Prime 6, and Spirit 6 (and a pool of Quintessence equal to their Essence). I think that would be the easiest conversion of Warp Reality to the Mage system, as Warp Reality can do things that even Masters have difficulty imagining.</span></span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What has a NC ever done that would be hard to replicate with all those spheres at 5?, do you have an example?.<br /> <br /> Because the description of Break Reality says that you need 5 successes at dif. 7 (almost impossible to get in one roll) to turn the surrounding air into mustard gas.And that's among the most powerful things the NC can do, according to the Charm, a fairly weak effect compared with what a Master of all those spheres can accomplish with rituals. Even if we do allow NC to make a &quot;ritual&quot; (extended roll for Break Reality), I don't remember anything a Crawler has ever done that would be difficult to duplicate with &quot;normal&quot; (1-5) level spheres.<br /> <br /> Let's not exagerate, it's better to leave the Archspheres for demon lords and other beings that can do things that are trully impossible with &quot;normal&quot; Spheres, like give Spheres to humans or take away Permanent Paradox. NC can do impressive things like turning the floor in molten silver, or a werewolf into mud, but that's nothing that can't be &quot;imagined&quot; with Spheres at 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think maybe it comes down to this. It's more of a game translation issue than anything else. If a NC were to appear in Mage instead of WtA, it should be given Sphere ratings (even if only virtual ones) to cover the concept of what they're supposed to do/be. I'd imagine they would also have a form of innate countermagic, given what they are/represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIf you treat Break Reality as a normal Charm then a mage could potentially take it away with Spirit 5, as that level can give new Charms to spirits (and what a mage can give, can also take).<br /> <br /> Fun fact, the reason why I didn't mentioned that option (to just remove the Charm entirely with Spirit 5) it's because I was treating that charm as something &quot;special&quot; all along. I don't think a mage should be able to just &quot;take&quot; or &quot;give&quot; the power to alter reality (or rather not without Archspheres)<br /> <br /> The thing you both fail to see it's that <b>is entirely possible to fuck the hability to use True Magick</b>. By the rules, you can do it with Prime 2 (increase difficulty), or with minor wards (take dice away from all the actions of target group). And these are relatively weak magics, they don't even imply a full understanding of how magick works. It's not all that hard to impair the power to alter reality.<br /> <br /> As for the Lore, I do count seeing a NC warping reality with Spirit 1 + Prime 1 or whatever as a form of &quot;research&quot; that justify gaining that particular piece of Lore. Also mage could &quot;revive&quot; the encounter from different perspectives with Time 2 + Prime/Spirit 1 (even the parts that she didn't experienced directly), consult Past Lives, the endless well of knowledge that it's the Dream, and/or consult wise spirits. Mages don't lack knowledge sources to discover anything that would be needed to know to craft a Rote. Obviously, not every mage would know how to do it, but I think it's far from impossible to discover","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-13-2017, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T07:26:04-07:00","id":1103121,"title":"","content":"Well, a NC can turn a Garou's marrow into plutonium, which would be a Life 3, Spirit 3, and Matter 5 effect in Mage. Now, the exact limit to Warp Reality is up to the individual ST, but I tend to be pretty liberal with what a NC is capable of doing with Warp Reality, and I tend to think that they can transform anything into anything within the limits of Reality as defined by WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T09:27:35-07:00","id":1103165,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it, I could see giving them the 6 level just as an easy way to justify more potent effects for less successes (as, NC recive 2 successes per Arete success). Because you can't really do that much with Arete 6 in one turn (magick it's rather weak for those that can't/won't use rituals). Of course, giving them more Arete, and lowering the difficulty, could work too.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;what&quot; should they be able to do, I don't think the Charm should allow for impossibles. NC shouldn't be able to create new races of Fera, cure the Curse of Caine or Awaken people into Nephandism. They would be much more relevant than the engines of horrid destruction that they are if they were able to reproduce Incarna (or above) level &quot;effects&quot; on a regular basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-13-2017, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T11:25:09-07:00","id":1103220,"title":"","content":"Personally I think giving them level 6+ Spheres is a bit much. But several Spheres at 5 with a high Arete would replicate the Charm fine I would think. Whatever works out to giving them around the same amount of net successes to achieve similar results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103114#post1103114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bIf you treat Break Reality as a normal Charm then a mage could potentially take it away with Spirit 5, as that level can give new Charms to spirits (and what a mage can give, can also take).<br /> <br /> Fun fact, the reason why I didn't mentioned that option (to just remove the Charm entirely with Spirit 5) it's because I was treating that charm as something &quot;special&quot; all along. I don't think a mage should be able to just &quot;take&quot; or &quot;give&quot; the power to alter reality (or rather not without Archspheres)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree it isn't a normal Charm, since no other spirit type has access to it from what I remember. After all, it's specifically listed under just the Nexus Crawler entry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103114#post1103114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The thing you both fail to see it's that <b>is entirely possible to fuck the hability to use True Magick</b>. By the rules, you can do it with Prime 2 (increase difficulty), or with minor wards (take dice away from all the actions of target group). And these are relatively weak magics, they don't even imply a full understanding of how magick works. It's not all that hard to impair the power to alter reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I realize that just fine. And I think that's a flaw in the system. In broad strokes, I think Mage works fine. But once you get to specifics like this, Mages either have no powers (countered like you said) or unlimited powers (using Rituals). And when it comes to crossover (which this really is at this point), Mage auto-wins everything because the Magick system is only set up to go against itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103114#post1103114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for the Lore, I do count seeing a NC warping reality with Spirit 1 + Prime 1 or whatever as a form of &quot;research&quot; that justify gaining that particular piece of Lore. Also mage could &quot;revive&quot; the encounter from different perspectives with Time 2 + Prime/Spirit 1 (even the parts that she didn't experienced directly), consult Past Lives, the endless well of knowledge that it's the Dream, and/or consult wise spirits. Mages don't lack knowledge sources to discover anything that would be needed to know to craft a Rote. Obviously, not every mage would know how to do it, but I think it's far from impossible to discover</div> </div> </div> </div>You are talking about the knowledge to know what dice pool is being rolled to use what power. That is purely a mechanics thing and doesn't really have a place in-character imo. It's one thing to shut down the power via countermagic or by raising difficulties. It's entirely another to target a specific dice pool imo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103165#post1103165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for &quot;what&quot; should they be able to do, I don't think the Charm should allow for impossibles. NC shouldn't be able to create new races of Fera, cure the Curse of Caine or Awaken people into Nephandism. They would be much more relevant than the engines of horrid destruction that they are if they were able to reproduce Incarna (or above) level &quot;effects&quot; on a regular basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree that Warp Reality shouldn't be able to do any of those things. They are way outside of the description given for the Charm. The changes are supposed to be instant transformations. Not cures or curses or creations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T11:50:18-07:00","id":1103228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103220#post1103220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are talking about the knowledge to know what dice pool is being rolled to use what power. That is purely a mechanics thing and doesn't really have a place in-character imo. It's one thing to shut down the power via countermagic or by raising difficulties. It's entirely another to target a specific dice pool imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can easily see Mages of many types - from Technocrats through Hermetics to Dreamspeakers - agreeing that, once a Nexus Crawler is observed through appropriate means, it becomes clearly visible that it's [insert term(s) that a given Mage uses for Nexus Crawler's Willpower] is linked to it's ability to warp reality. (Or something along these lines.) The rules crunch has a reflection in-universe, I'd say.<br /> Especially as Willpower is a constantly used trait, often as a defense against True Magick and other supernatural abilities. Mages should be familiar with it, even if one Mage might call it by many different names and/or see it from many perspectives and facets.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T14:26:40-07:00","id":1103279,"title":"","content":"Well, Mages can be shut down by Sorcerers and practitioners a Blood Magic pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T16:59:00-07:00","id":1103328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I realize that just fine. And I think that's a flaw in the system. In broad strokes, I think Mage works fine. But once you get to specifics like this, Mages either have no powers (countered like you said) or(using Rituals). And when it comes to crossover (which this really is at this point), Mage auto-wins everything because the Magick system is only set up to go against itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're mentioning (Arete system making rituals OP) it's a problem that Mage certainly has. But it has nothing to do with the methods we were just discussing.<br /> <br /> Ritual abuse it's to gather a Cult, other mages, and use conjunctional magick to get a ton of successes, allowing overcome any problem and any defense by brute strenght. Bonus points if you made the ritual in your &quot;off time&quot; between plays.<br /> <br /> Mages have two ways of overcoming odds: Brute force ritual, and sidestep the issue. And the favored option in Mage books it's always the second one. Don't face the obstacle, surround it with versatility.<br /> <br /> If you face a mage with a super powerful Kinetic shield, you don't go to your home to gather enough successes to pierce it with your katana. What you do it's to throw a lightining bolt (after checking, perhaps, with Forces 1 that the shield doesn't protect against that).<br /> The methods that we were discussing (anti-magic/countermagic/arguably, to alter it's attributes) are more in tune with this second approach. The idea it's to understand how the enemy works (It can be harder or easier, but magick should help), and then disable it by exploiting a weakness.<br /> <br /> As I have stated early, impairing the skill to Break Reality it's hardly an instant win. A NC doesn't need that Charm to kill mages, brute strenght works just fine. On the other hand even Werewolf says that the reality warping powers of mages are &quot;similar to that of powerful spirits&quot;. Having that in mind, the idea of mages countering the NC with their &quot;similar&quot; powers doesn't seem that out of character to me.<br /> <br /> Countering the NC reality warping with their own it's, I think, what mages can bring to the table without using cheesy rituals. But, ironically, the idea that a mage can do something like that seems to be much more reviled than suggesting to pille 52 or so sucesses in an artifact to one shot the damn thing. There's certainly a flaw in the system here, but it isn't the &quot;unlimited power&quot; of rituals (not this time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-13-2017, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T17:40:09-07:00","id":1103337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1102909#post1102909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think maybe it comes down to this. It's more of a game translation issue than anything else. If a NC were to appear in Mage instead of WtA, it should be given Sphere ratings (even if only virtual ones) to cover the concept of what they're supposed to do/be. I'd imagine they would also have a form of innate countermagic, given what they are/represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is accurate or necessary. In M20 there are several incredibly powerful spirits (Grand Natura is the first that comes to mind) that follow the exact same rules as spirits in Werewolf. There's no need to assign spheres at all; you just use it as is and it works fine. This thread is the first I'm hearing of spirits in Mage using spheres at all. I'm wondering if this is an older rule that was updated in M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T20:11:54-07:00","id":1103366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103328#post1103328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What you're mentioning (Arete system making rituals OP) it's a problem that Mage certainly has. But it has nothing to do with the methods we were just discussing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for that tangent. I was just using Rituals as one example of how the crossover system breaks down when involving Mage. Alternatively, Mages can raise the difs for just about everything with little in the way of required Spheres. That accomplishes near the same level of system abuse.<br /> <br /> Ritual abuse it's to gather a Cult, other mages, and use conjunctional magick to get a ton of successes, allowing overcome any problem and any defense by brute strenght. Bonus points if you made the ritual in your &quot;off time&quot; between plays.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103328#post1103328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you face a mage with a super powerful Kinetic shield, you don't go to your home to gather enough successes to pierce it with your katana. What you do it's to throw a lightining bolt (after checking, perhaps, with Forces 1 that the shield doesn't protect against that).</div> </div> </div> </div>In that example though, there is literally no reason for that shield not to protect against lightning as well since it requires the same Sphere to do (Forces). So (in my experience) the Mage player will just have all energy protections as well. Nevermind that doing it that way <i>should</i> conflict with Paradigms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103328#post1103328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As I have stated early, impairing the skill to Break Reality it's hardly an instant win. A NC doesn't need that Charm to kill mages, brute strenght works just fine. On the other hand even Werewolf says that the reality warping powers of mages are &quot;similar to that of powerful spirits&quot;. Having that in mind, the idea of mages countering the NC with their &quot;similar&quot; powers doesn't seem that out of character to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that countering a NC with similar powers is in line thematically. In reference to specifically countering Warp Reality by lowering their dice pool though is having a Mage character specifically tweak the meta-mechanics of the game system. That I don't see as thematically appropriate. Mind you, I am also more than willing to drop this portion of the conversation since it seems to me to possibly be a waste of time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103328#post1103328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Countering the NC reality warping with their own it's, I think, what mages can bring to the table without using cheesy rituals. But, ironically, the idea that a mage can do something like that seems to be much more reviled than suggesting to pille 52 or so sucesses in an artifact to one shot the damn thing. There's certainly a flaw in the system here, but it isn't the &quot;unlimited power&quot; of rituals (not this time).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends a lot on how it's gone about. A Mage being resourceful and tweaking a situation (lets say by altering probabilities/difficulties) can add a lot to a scene. A Mage lowering the Willpower of a NC to make its signature power unusable is too meta for my tastes.<br /> <br /> It'd be like similar to using Magick to lower a Vampire's Discipline dice pool as opposed to countering said Discipline or protecting against it in advance. The way it's gone about just bothers me. And obviously that sort of thing is going to be perfectly acceptable in some circles. I just wouldn't allow it in my games.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T08:55:00-07:00","id":1103512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, Mages can raise the difs for just about everything with little in the way of required Spheres. That accomplishes near the same level of system abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then Dominate another supernatural it's a form of sytem abuse because supernaturals don't have Generation to fend themselves. Using the Gift to break technology in order to disable Hit-Marks it's a system abuse because Primium should block disabling magic. AND, finally, NC huge Essence lifebar and Rage it's a form of system abuse because most splats can't dish nor resist as much damage as a Werewolf pack. Games ain't balanced. We should restrict this thread to Werewolf then, because NC are balanced with Garou in mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that example though, there is literally no reason for that shield not to protect against lightning as well since it requires the same Sphere to do (Forces). So (in my experience) the Mage player will just have all energy protections as well. Nevermind that doing it that way <i>should</i> conflict with Paradigms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a discussion about this in the Mage forum some time ago. I think this is <i>possible </i>(with enough rituals), but I don't think this would be so easy.<br /> To my understanding, each different energy type should count as a different efffect (that CAN be cast as one rote, but increasing the number of successes needed). A kinetick barrier would feel very different than a sound-proof barrier. You don't see mages blasting with all forms of energies at once, instead they choose what to use. If you think about it, you don't often see mages affecting every energy at the same time, for instance, the Darksight rote implies that you have to choose what energy to percevie (I think it uses the word OR between the various energies that it detects). This is, as many things are, debatable. The way I interpret the rules, an absolute shielding can't be done so easily.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, if the protection it's that absolute then you can detect it and shot a Quintessence blast instead, or a psychic blast. Generally, a Mage won't be protected against everything because of how stacking persistent effects work. Especially if each one requires a massive ritual to be sure that it resists most attacks. General defenses do exist, but usually are easier to break and are treated as a big deal (things like Primium).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it depends a lot on how it's gone about. A Mage being resourceful and tweaking a situation (lets say by altering probabilities/difficulties) can add a lot to a scene. A Mage lowering the Willpower of a NC to make its signature power unusable is too meta for my tastes.<br /> <br /> It'd be like similar to using Magick to lower a Vampire's Discipline dice pool as opposed to countering said Discipline or protecting against it in advance. The way it's gone about just bothers me. And obviously that sort of thing is going to be perfectly acceptable in some circles. I just wouldn't allow it in my games. </div> </div> </div>I get that, and it's true...to some extent. It's not unlike when Demons use their Apocaliptic Forms to cast Lores more easily, or Lasombra increasing Manipulation to be better at Obtenebration. Players know that the Trait helps the particular power. But does the character knows that's how things work?.<br /> <br /> Some people feel that this kind of stuff it's a bad form of metagaming and should be frowned upon. \u200bI'm not so sure, one could argue that the Traits exist in game, and thus anyone who uses them should know, if only for experience, that certain forms reinforce certain powers, that being manipulative it's desirable for anyone wanting to master the dak powers...etc.<br /> <br /> Now, Spirit 5 allows to create whole spirits with all and Charms (as long as the latter are whitin the reach of the Spheres) out of ambient ephemera, and thus should allow to understand to some extent what does each spiritual Trait &quot;do&quot; (just like you understand that it's important to add Physical attributes to create a strong fighter). Understanding how Traits and Charms interact it's in that ballpark, otherwise you're crafting the spirit while being blind to it's potential (wich isn't very mage-y). That Blast it's affected by Rage should be comon knowledge at that point, if we accept that the Trait exists somehow in game if only to optimize a Blasting spirit. Break Reality...I can accept it's more esoteric, you need to make the jump from &quot;static&quot; spiritual powers to &quot;dynamic&quot; ones. It could be subject for some serious research, probably very dangerous, but not outside what a character could imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-14-2017, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T11:38:24-07:00","id":1103558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103512#post1103512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then Dominate another supernatural it's a form of sytem abuse because supernaturals don't have Generation to fend themselves. Using the Gift to break technology in order to disable Hit-Marks it's a system abuse because Primium should block disabling magic. AND, finally, NC huge Essence lifebar and Rage it's a form of system abuse because most splats can't dish nor resist as much damage as a Werewolf pack. Games ain't balanced. We should restrict this thread to Werewolf then, because NC are balanced with Garou in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are actually points repeatedly brought up in crossovers. The games weren't designed to interact with each other and so nothing is balanced against each other I agree. NCs were set up specifically to be Garou Antagonists and that adds a lot to why they don't necessarily translate well into other games. I have said in an earlier post that I think it ends up being a translation issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103512#post1103512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I had a discussion about this in the Mage forum some time ago. I think this is <i>possible </i>(with enough rituals), but I don't think this would be so easy.<br /> To my understanding, each different energy type should count as a different efffect (that CAN be cast as one rote, but increasing the number of successes needed). A kinetick barrier would feel very different than a sound-proof barrier. You don't see mages blasting with all forms of energies at once, instead they choose what to use. If you think about it, you don't often see mages affecting every energy at the same time, for instance, the Darksight rote implies that you have to choose what energy to percevie (I think it uses the word OR between the various energies that it detects). This is, as many things are, debatable. The way I interpret the rules, an absolute shielding can't be done so easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually agree with this 100%. Was just pointing out that I've seen Mage players (irl and on these forums) argue the opposite at times. Which in my opinion just kind of ignores the fluff and leans on their interpretations of the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103512#post1103512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I get that, and it's true...to some extent. It's not unlike when Demons use their Apocaliptic Forms to cast Lores more easily, or Lasombra increasing Manipulation to be better at Obtenebration. Players know that the Trait helps the particular power. But does the character knows that's how things work?.<br /> <br /> Some people feel that this kind of stuff it's a bad form of metagaming and should be frowned upon. \u200bI'm not so sure, one could argue that the Traits exist in game, and thus anyone who uses them should know, if only for experience, that certain forms reinforce certain powers, that being manipulative it's desirable for anyone wanting to master the dak powers...etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This leads to the possibility of attacking someone's occult rating so that they cant use any (well, most) of their Obten powers which I think is silly and Meta. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103512#post1103512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now, Spirit 5 allows to create whole spirits with all and Charms (as long as the latter are whitin the reach of the Spheres) out of ambient ephemera, and thus should allow to understand to some extent what does each spiritual Trait &quot;do&quot; (just like you understand that it's important to add Physical attributes to create a strong fighter). Understanding how Traits and Charms interact it's in that ballpark, otherwise you're crafting the spirit while being blind to it's potential (wich isn't very mage-y). That Blast it's affected by Rage should be comon knowledge at that point, if we accept that the Trait exists somehow in game if only to optimize a Blasting spirit. Break Reality...I can accept it's more esoteric, you need to make the jump from &quot;static&quot; spiritual powers to &quot;dynamic&quot; ones. It could be subject for some serious research, probably very dangerous, but not outside what a character could imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I don't like the overall idea that Spirits are made up of only 4 traits (5 with Charms). I think that's very much a system for us the players and not for the characters. The concept that every spirit in existence (outside of super special ones with Spheres, only in Mage) are made up of 3 sliding scales from 1 to 10, a pool of Essence points and a small list of Charms is unimaginable in game I would think. Or at least I see it that way. Because Spirits are never characters, we've been given a simplified system to run them that doesn't do much to give them complexity.<br /> <br /> By the system, any spirit under Incarna level is just as susceptible to the Mage attack strategies mentioned which make little sense (and Incarna are only above that because they don't have real stats to attack). It is only slightly harder to disable a NC than a pattern spider. I do think there were some implied difficulty scaling (needing more successes) based on spirit power level. And that was mentioned earlier in the thread, but I don't know where that would be written or even what edition. But either way, that's left up to the ST to decide how and when to apply it, so that's not exactly a hard rule to my knowledge (a lot of Mage Sphere power levels aren't).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T13:21:39-07:00","id":1103593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103337#post1103337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think this is accurate or necessary. In M20 there are several incredibly powerful spirits (Grand Natura is the first that comes to mind) that follow the exact same rules as spirits in Werewolf. There's no need to assign spheres at all; you just use it as is and it works fine. This thread is the first I'm hearing of spirits in Mage using spheres at all. I'm wondering if this is an older rule that was updated in M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I've seen an Incarna/Aeon statted up with sphere magic at an extremely high level, but I think that was back in 2nd or even 1st Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T17:02:59-07:00","id":1103656,"title":"","content":"1rst ED, Book of Madness, the Aeon had Arete 10 and all Spheres at 5 when Materialized in it's most powerful form. However, it was supposed to be much more powerful that that (and in the realm of being &quot;beyond Traits&quot;) when encountered in the Umbra, making one suspect that those weren't the Traits of the Incarna, but of one of his avatars. In that same book you have the stats of a powerful minion of that spirit (a Lady, a powerful Jagglin in Werewolf terms) that also had Spheres.<br /> <br /> In the Digital Web you have an AI that has Spheres too, and seems to be a spirit of some kind. There could be one or two examples that I don't remember.<br /> <br /> It wasn't common, that's for sure. You can say that is an old rule that was updated for M20. I still believe that giving spheres to the NC has merit. NC never were presented in Mage as far as I can remember, are at the Jagglin level, and have a power that alters rerality. They fill all the requisites as far as I'm concerned","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-14-2017, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T17:11:12-07:00","id":1103658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1103656#post1103656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1rst ED, Book of Madness, the Aeon had Arete 10 and all Spheres at 5 when Materialized in it's most powerful form. However, it was supposed to be much more powerful that that (and in the realm of being &quot;beyond Traits&quot;) when encountered in the Umbra, making one suspect that those weren't the Traits of the Incarna, but of one of his avatars. In that same book you have the stats of a powerful minion of that spirit (a Lady, a powerful Jagglin in Werewolf terms) that also had Spheres.<br /> <br /> In the Digital Web you have an AI that has Spheres too, and seems to be a spirit of some kind. There could be one or two examples that I don't remember.<br /> <br /> It wasn't common, that's for sure. You can say that is an old rule that was updated for M20. I still believe that giving spheres to the NC has merit. NC never were presented in Mage as far as I can remember, are at the Jagglin level, and have a power that alters rerality. They fill all the requisites as far as I'm concerned</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems to me warp reality is easier to use for purposes of a Nexus Crawler than &quot;All spheres at 5&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T17:56:21-07:00","id":1103675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This leads to the possibility of attacking someone's occult rating so that they cant use any (well, most) of their Obten powers which I think is silly and Meta.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the rules of M20, if a mage use an Ability as an Instrument, the mage needs to have at least as many points in that Ability as the highest Sphere level used. Thus, if a Virtual Adept uses his mad hacking skillz to alter reality, he needs having points in Computer or some form of Science. Would it be silly to impair his magical hacking by removing all his knowledge about computers?.<br /> <br /> He knows (because spheres) that altering the &quot;source code&quot; of a human to transform it into another being it's possible, but now he can't even understand C++ for beginners, much less the esoteric coding he normaly uses to override reality. I think it would be silier to say that this kind of damage won't impair his magick at all.<br /> <br /> Now, you know what IS silly. It's silly that the trivia about Area 51 and Crowley that you had as a mortal (IOC reason to have Occult) somehow makes you better at manipulating supernatural shadow.<br /> <br /> You think that removing Occult to impair Obtenebration it's silly, but I think that this perceived silliness it's just an extention of the inherent absurdity of the system that the majority of WoD uses to activate it's powers. A system that you use literally all the time, in spite of it's inherent sillines.<br /> <br /> If getting better at &quot;Jam Technology&quot; by increasing your Crafts skill isn't terribly silly to begin with, then why would be silly to get worse at it if you loose that Skill that was helping your power?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I have said in an earlier post that I think it ends up being a translation issue.</b><br /> ...<br /> Eh. I don't like the overall idea that Spirits are made up of only 4 traits (5 with Charms). I think that's very much a system for us the players and not for the characters. The concept that every spirit in existence (<b>outside of super special ones with Spheres, only in Mage</b>) are made up of 3 sliding scales from 1 to 10, a pool of Essence points and a small list of Charms is unimaginable in game I would think. Or at least I see it that way. Because Spirits are never characters, we've been given a simplified system to run them that doesn't do much to give them complexity.<br /> <br /> By the system, any spirit under Incarna level is just as susceptible to the Mage attack strategies mentioned which make little sense (and Incarna are only above that because they don't have real stats to attack). It is only slightly harder to disable a NC than a pattern spider. I do think there were some implied difficulty scaling (needing more successes) based on spirit power level. And that was mentioned earlier in the thread, but I don't know where that would be written or even what edition. But either way, that's left up to the ST to decide how and when to apply it, so that's not exactly a hard rule to my knowledge (a lot of Mage Sphere power levels aren't).</div> </div> </div> </div>The system it's what it is, and when a mage casts a spell it's better to base the rules arround that system. But I want to concentrate on the traduction of NC to mage:<br /> <br /> I'm all in when it comes to &quot;translate&quot; NC to Sphere System, but this doesn't mean that you can't disable them. This it's what I was trying to highlight when I said that<i> &quot;it's entirelly possible to fuck True Magick in Mage&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> If you do give NC True Magick, then fine, you won't gain a lot by supressing NC Willpower (wich doesn't mean that reducing NC Traits isn't going to be useful, because these do influence it's fighting prowess), but then you have to use the rules of True Magick. Arguably, TM could be easier to &quot;supress&quot;, and you don't get to argue that doing this would require 3 successes per Atribute instead of 1, nor phenomenal Lore, because the kind of things that would fuck TM are very well know, and have rules.<br /> <br /> Which goes to the second part of your argument...maybe ther are rules about &quot;power level&quot; (probably not in Mage books), maybe there aren't, but you need to understand that it would go contrary of how most of Mage works.<br /> If you don't want to have translation issues, then learn the languaje. Mage isn't about &quot;power levels&quot;, a Master isn't much harder to supress than a starting character, if caught unprepared. Arete increases very slowly, and Spheres usualy give versatility more than power, the big exception being the super rare and polemical Arch-levels. This isn't vampire, where an Elder it's always going to have the edge. Rules are supposed to be more or less universal regardless of your &quot;power level&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-14-2017, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T10:26:20-07:00","id":1110910,"title":"","content":"Drop 35 successes worth of antimatter into the umbra. Anything on that side of the gauntlet within a mile of the detonation point takes roughly 100 points of aggravated damage with no possible soak.<br /> <br /> Antimatter is amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T16:57:52-07:00","id":1111066,"title":"","content":"Mage is amazing, because impossible is not a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T17:35:06-07:00","id":1111074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1110910#post1110910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Drop 35 successes worth of antimatter into the umbra. Anything on that side of the gauntlet within a mile of the detonation point takes roughly 100 points of aggravated damage with no possible soak.<br /> <br /> Antimatter is amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it wouldn't, because the ephemera composing spiritual existence isn't matter. This, setting aside how I'm guessing there's probably a horrid mismatch between Mage mechanics for creating shit and the damage of a significantly large mutual annihilation m/am reaction, what with a boring, normal nuke having a damage of Really? and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T17:44:36-07:00","id":1111078,"title":"","content":"Matter is easy to get, and just as easy to dump across the gauntlet with the antimatter.<br /> <br /> To be fair, 35 successes worth of antimatter is not a lot of antimatter. Even with that much it's still microscopic amounts. But Antimatter has specific rules in the Sons of Ether rev book. 30 successes to sink in to preperation, then you can spend successes on actually creating antimatter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T18:51:03-07:00","id":1111099,"title":"","content":"It requires 20 successes and then deals three health levels of aggravated damage per success (which is unsoakable by material objects). The problem is that nothing is material in the Umbra, so everything can soak the damage in the Umbra, and there is nothing about how antimatter-matter reactions function in the Umbra (there is nothing about weak force nuclear interactions in the Umbra in any of the books). I would personally rule that antimatter-matter reactions produce an equivalent amount of ice cream in the Umbra, because it makes as much sense as anything else in the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T21:29:50-07:00","id":1111146,"title":"","content":"Would ephemera even be affected by the explosion if it didn't involve an additional effect to spirit-charge it? I know I've seen a rote that turns a person's body to ephemera without crossing the gauntlet, and it leaves them visible but completely intangible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T07:59:46-07:00","id":1111267,"title":"","content":"As Aya stated, anttimater does successes x 3 of damage that have to be counted after you got all the 20 successes you need to create the stuff (the first 20 don't count), you also may need a few successes on Duration because this is a Revised Rote. Anttimater rote conpensates this by quickly escalating in both damage and area of effect, so, it's a good Rote and not gamebreaking at all in my opinion.<br /> <br /> There's a much more gamebreaking Rote in Spirit Ways that uses a bunch of spheres at 3 (I owe you which), it's called &quot;Eat Spirit&quot;, and drains 5 Essence points from a Spirit per success. Basically, it's almost twice as powerful as Antimater, and could get the work done in 20 successes + whatever you need to hold it into a charm Of course, I guess that eating a Nexus Crawler isn't very healthy to your resonance, to say the least, but it would be a badass thing to do for a Nephandi.<br /> <br /> If you use Sorcerers Cruzade rules you have a Rote that does Successes x 4 (Prime 5/Forces 5, it's called Dragon's Fire or something like that), and any Rote can do Successes x 3 if you pass a certain threshold. So, as you see, this kind of damage isn't THAT rare in Mage, even without going to the almighty Forces 6 that does Successes x 4 +1 of damage. Really, there's nothing to see here, Antimater it's just a potent effect requiring lot's of successes.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, throwing such a thing against a <i>single </i>NC it's a waste of perfectly good antimater that could be used to blast a few starships or a small Realm.<br /> <br /> Now, to adress particular issues:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it wouldn't, because the ephemera composing spiritual existence isn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>IF you need matter to activate the explosion it would be trivial, at this power level, to transport some to the other side with the antimater. And this it's a big IF, because guns work if you travel with them to the Umbra in spite of the lack of oxigen (after being &quot;dedicated&quot; with all and bullets, or something like this, of course, but, again, doing this after creating a 35 + 20 successes nuke it's kinda trivial)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that nothing is material in the Umbra, so everything can soak the damage in the Umbra</div> </div> </div> </div>An area of effect , like an explosion, doesn't see its damage reduced just because someone soaks it. You need to have direct cover, and Umbral air doesn't count as cover against anything, as far as I know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and there is nothing about how antimatter-matter reactions function in the Umbra (there is nothing about weak force nuclear interactions in the Umbra in any of the books). </div> </div> </div>Wrong, we know that Forces works normaly trough most of the Umbra (as per every book from M20 to the Book of Worlds), you don't need to add Spirit to throw a fireball nor to fly with Forces. Forces 5 relates to weak nuclear force interactions and, by the RAW, these should work as well as the gravity thrusters of voidships or any other effect that employs &quot;science&quot;...Also we know that the Penumbra respects more or less the same laws as our world, gravity exists, a gun works. Of course, thowing energy arround in the Penumbra isn't the same as doing so in the Flux Realm. So, I'm open to antimater not working (or working differently) in bizarre realms that don't respect the laws pf physics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would ephemera even be affected by the explosion if it didn't involve an additional effect to spirit-charge it? I know I've seen a rote that turns a person's body to ephemera without crossing the gauntlet, and it leaves them visible but completely intangible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it would be affected, because, as I said, throwing a Forces effect, like a fireball, in the Umbra works normaly, it would be shitty to say that explosions don't work unless they have been blessed by the touch of the Forces Sphere (especially when it's stated that Matters 5 can act like Forces).<br /> <br /> This it's the way it has been for years, There's even a rote that throws a grenade to the Umbra in Guide of the Technocracy. You could think this is very similar, but with a bigger, meaner, grenade.<br /> <br /> There's even a mention in the Void Engineers Convention Book as using antimater against other voidships. Of course, you could say that this happened in Conventional Space, but &quot;normal&quot; outer space it's considered &quot;safe&quot; by void engineer standards, 99% of the time enemies are on the other side, thus, I would think that their weapons aren't designed to work in the matterial side.<br /> <br /> As for the weird Rote that transforms you into ephemera. It's a very rare reference, I think it wasn't mentioned more than one time...and it's a bit bizarre, you can't use Matter in the Umbra because there's no Matter there, even your body get's transformed into ephemera, BUT if you enter trough a Shalowing you're supposed to be entirely material in the Umbra, and yet able to affect and be affected by the environment, thus I don't know if that Rote it's valid anymore. All that I can say it's that interactions between ephemera and matter are rare, and that explosions work as usual.<br /> <br /> It could even be argued that antimater would turn into &quot;spiritual antimater&quot; when traversing the Gauntlet via Spirit, like everything else does, and in this case it would interact with ephemera as expected (by blowing up), just like everything else does when you do exactly the same. All in all, usually you don't need to ask if a material object will work in the Umbra, guns work, laptops lack power and internet, but work...why wouldn't antimater work?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-04-2017, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T08:24:54-07:00","id":1111275,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering of how effective would be to try to throw a net made of Primium to the NC. Having dice of general countermagic being rolled against you isn't as impressive nor deadly as a nuke but it may be quite impairing. Also, unlike a nuke, it can be used in the real world without colateral damage, multiple times, and against other kinds of foes, like, say, fleeing mages.<br /> <br /> Because, let's face it, NC aren't a common treath, I imagine most mages DO go out of their homes without their &quot;35+ successes NC blaster&quot;, on the grounds that NC are less of a realistic treath than other mages or even vampires, and mages or vampirees don't require that level of firepower to be put down.<br /> <br /> However, I'm not convinced of the efficiency of a net as a weapon. It isn't very useful if the opponent can throw it away in one action. An Effect or two could be added to make the net more efficient, but having to add a lot of Effects to make it less useless takes away from it's elegance as a weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-04-2017, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T10:24:24-07:00","id":1111330,"title":"","content":"There is an actual question of how effective antimatter would be as a weapon (or as a propulsion system) because only electron-positron interactions release pure energy. When you get into the physics, antiproton-proton reactions produce pions and kaons, the pions and kaons decay into muons, and the muons decay into positrons, neutrinos, and electrons (and the positrons and electrons explode when they interact). Since the resulting particles are going at around 99.999% c, they tend to travel very, very far before they decay because of time dilation effects. While pions and kaons only have a halflife of about 12-25 nanoseconds, muons have a halflife of about 2.2 microseconds and, when you calculate the normal time dilation effects, that means that the muons travel for 46.2 microseconds before they experience 2.2 microseconds of decay, meaning that they have traveled nearly 14 kilometers from their point of annihilation (when they explode with a force of over 40,000 metric tons of TNT per gram of antimatter). In effect, you would need kilograms of antimatter before you could do any significant damage to anyone who was at the point of annihilation (though humans would probably suffer lethal levels of radiation from pion and muon interactions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T15:37:44-07:00","id":1111428,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> : So the rules may not be simulating our real world correctly ?...which in WoD it's a given.<br /> <br /> If you search you may notice that basic rules in many WoD games disrespect science even more than antimater here...Just ask your local simulationists: I.E: Falling damage it's very unrealistic for humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a much more gamebreaking Rote in Spirit Ways that uses a bunch of spheres at 3 (I owe you which), it's called &quot;Eat Spirit&quot;, and drains 5 Essence points from a Spirit per success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, the Rote it's not in Spirit Ways, but in the Tradition Book: Dreamspeakers (revised). It's called Spirit Eating and uses Mind 3, Prime 3, Spirit 2. And it's system It's a bit (a lot) more complicated than that. Basically, you enhance a weapon (that can be symbolic, like a piece of crystal or rattlers) to cause a certain amount of aggravated damage to the spirit. After that, every success of damage drains a point of Quintessence and drains 5 points of Power. There's a lot more, including a chance to gain a Mental Flaw, and it seems to be the spirit (no pun intended) of it's rules that you do all the damage in one action (no rituals), albeit this isn't clearly stated.<br /> It's a bit too poweful for those sphere levels, as M20 states that you can't drain a spirit's Essence with less than Spirit 4/Prime 4.So, nowdays the spell woud require at least Mind 3, Prime 4, Spirit 4 (maybe a little more, if you ask me, and perhaps a small threshold that you need to pass before getting to the damage or something like that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-04-2017, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T06:08:46-07:00","id":1111630,"title":"","content":"Since we already hit pretty high sphere levels why not have a charm ready with the command \u201cServe me\u201c or something to that effect.<br /> <br /> Mind and Spirit 4 plus Prime 2 or 3 depending on Tass.<br /> It is useful for other purposes as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T18:43:40-07:00","id":1111928,"title":"","content":"Well, it's feasible, but doesn't need to be any easier.<br /> <br /> Even exorcizing or summoning a being of the power of a NC requires arround 20 successes (it's on the &quot;potent Bane&quot; category, close to Lord, 20 succeses to exorcise in 2nd ed, and that's just a &quot;leave!&quot;), I imagine that a Binding one into submission would be much harder, there's a reason why even Hermetics &quot;bargain&quot; (in their own fashion).<br /> <br /> And it's all or nothing, if you fail by a split hair you can't compensate throwing another fireball.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-05-2017, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T00:00:43-07:00","id":1111996,"title":"","content":"Still a whopping 15 successes less than antimatter. And it is not so prone to collateral damage, mishandling and you can use it against intangible i.e. Astral spirits as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T04:00:02-07:00","id":1112034,"title":"","content":"True, antimatter it's better deployed against many NC. Each extra NC you have increases the efficiency of that approach. And preferably somewhere you don't care to destroy everything in a mile (perhaps that's why it's used in the Deep Umbra, where a Nephandi flesh starship with a flock of Banes isn't so rare)<br /> <br /> As other alternative:<br /> <br /> You could create two or so Talisman weapons with a Spirit Eating Effect to dual wield like the<b> B@DA$$</b> you are (or just (<i>yawn</i>) give them to your companions)<br /> <br /> Attaking with them would cause significative damage to any spirit, as it causes normal weapon damage (or alternatively, normal magick damage, wich may be better or not), and then 5 extra per level inflicted (so, if you manage to inflict 9 aggravated after soaking, the spirit will lose 54 Essence, more than enough to kill a small NC with a single strike). These weapons would be very effective against spirits of all types and can be used against spirits that are possesing something too.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't kill the bane in the first two strikes, which I dare to say it's feasible for a dedicated combat bane-eater shaman that has reached the power to create these to begin with, you can still cast a spell becuase Talismans do not consume a magical action.<br /> <br /> You would also get a load of evil Quintessence (that can be stored in the weapon and you may want to purify before using it to create more powerful Talismans to use against Nexus Crawlers), and if you drestroy the Bane, which it's more than likely, it's gone forever, no reform, and you can get evil knowledge from it, that may drive you <i>maaad</i> or not (possibly, removing the Mind 3 requisite would avoid this latter effect, that's surely more desirable for Nephandi than for a Bane Eater Shaman...then again, if you want Bane Lore, this is how you get Bane Lore).<br /> <br /> Also, since this it's a Rote, it has rules. You may not agree with them, you may think that they shit on the general rules of magick and everything sacred, but it is as canon and clear as any Thaumaturgic Ritual. And yes, you could Ritual Spirit Eating to massive effect, but I think this approach it's more in tune with the spirit of the rules for that Rote <i>and, as a shaman, you wouldn't want to disrespect the spirit of the rules, right? </i><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-06-2017, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T22:15:20-07:00","id":1113111,"title":"","content":"How strong is a nexus crawler? Antediluvian level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T22:50:01-07:00","id":1113123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1113111#post1113111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How strong is a nexus crawler? Antediluvian level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, but a NC has essentially a little plot device charm (break reality) and in some cases over 100 power. <br /> Plus it has pretty high stats.<br /> <br /> But, as in most cases, anything with comparable power to an ancient 3rd gen would wipe the floor with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T04:15:40-07:00","id":1113178,"title":"","content":"Indeed.<br /> <br /> Adding to that:<br /> <br /> In the spiritual hierarchy Nexus Crawlers are strong Jagglings. In Mage they would be arguably on Lord level, albeit Lords tend to be unique creatures.<br /> <br /> In the spiritual &quot;power scale&quot;, these are the levels just below &quot;godlike being without stats&quot;. They're considerably stronger than your average demon summoning.<br /> <br /> In that sense I think they're relativistic to a Mathusalem/Archmage, but that's just my opinion. &quot;Power levels&quot; can't really be compared as mages, vampires and spirits work very differently.<br /> <br /> NC tend to be loners, as even other Banes fear them (that's not to say that they can't appear with other Banes, but rather than they aren't the &quot;commander of the troops&quot; type. If they apear with other Banes, worse for the Banes).<br /> They don't use what one would call &quot;a strategy&quot; (not that they need to do that, they're mighty, but Werewolf says that if NC cared to fight with strategy, Garou would be long dead) and are extremely unpredictable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-08-2017, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T04:41:30-07:00","id":1113184,"title":"","content":"Throw a vampire at it and trick the crawler into possessing them. The crawler will quickly learn that they are now screwed (since banes can't control vampires, can't leave their bodies and will die with the vampire). Then the werewolves show up and see some caitif vampire running after the crawler, yelling &quot;GET INSIDE MY BELLY!&quot; <br /> (This is obviously a joke, I know that NCs would probably rip the vampire a new one, but I find it hilarious)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T07:46:36-07:00","id":1113243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1113184#post1113184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throw a vampire at it and trick the crawler into possessing them. The crawler will quickly learn that they are now screwed (since banes can't control vampires, can't leave their bodies and will die with the vampire). Then the werewolves show up and see some caitif vampire running after the crawler, yelling &quot;GET INSIDE MY BELLY!&quot;<br /> (This is obviously a joke, I know that NCs would probably rip the vampire a new one, but I find it hilarious)</div> </div> </div> </div>Crawlers are powerful and alien enough that they probably share the ability of the psychomachiae and blood banes to make vampires their cars. That is, on the rare occasion when you meet one that has that Charm; by default, they do not possess hosts and act as tenets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T12:50:43-07:00","id":1113332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1113243#post1113243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Crawlers are powerful and alien enough that they probably share the ability of the psychomachiae and blood banes to make vampires their cars. That is, on the rare occasion when you meet one that has that Charm; by default, they do not possess hosts and act as tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I know, but I find the idea hillarious...<br /> In a serious confrontation, my characters (mostly Vampires and Changelings) would fight them as they fight werewolves: No at all! I usually play diplomats and leaders and overall non-combatants. If a confrontation is inevitable, they would die... probably gloriously, but die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T19:18:35-07:00","id":1118797,"title":"","content":"Maybe my players and I were doing something wrong, but using canon Nexus Crawlers never seemed like that big of a deal. They were pretty easy to defeat unless I cheated for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T13:44:17-07:00","id":1119064,"title":"","content":"How were you using it?, what was done to kill the NC?. I've heard about 4th gen Mathusalems being defeated with total ease, it all depends on how you ST them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T16:15:59-07:00","id":1123218,"title":"","content":"In a mixed party... Have the local Amalgam open fire on it while our motley Raises the Ire and attacks,make popcorn and watch while the Marauder violate the Precepts of Damian again, elsewhere the NWO Opertaive psionically sets it on fire with Forces while the Garou tear it to shreds, the sole remaining human in our game wards it with Faith long enough for our kubera to use Fertile Mind on it to increase the Nexus Crawler's pain. Lastly, feed it to the redcap. Laugh as she shrugs off Wyrm Taint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T19:54:52-07:00","id":1123280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1123218#post1123218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a mixed party... Have the local Amalgam open fire on it while our motley Raises the Ire and attacks,make popcorn and watch while the Marauder violate the Precepts of Damian again, elsewhere the NWO Opertaive psionically sets it on fire with Forces while the Garou tear it to shreds, the sole remaining human in our game wards it with Faith long enough for our kubera to use Fertile Mind on it to increase the Nexus Crawler's pain. Lastly, feed it to the redcap. Laugh as she shrugs off Wyrm Taint.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... don't think this would happen. I\u2019m not one to say &quot;you're playing the game wrong &quot; but if such an occurrence is even possible in your game you're definitely not playing it as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T01:43:20-07:00","id":1123363,"title":"","content":"There is no intention other than to have fun.<br /> Ergo they play as intended \ud83d\ude09","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T18:44:07-07:00","id":1124566,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* Anything that gets in the way of fun gets tossed. Everyone's either related, dating, married, oathbound to, or working with someone else in our various groups. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T15:22:46-07:00","id":1124970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1100429-how-would-your-character-or-splat-fight-a-nexus-crawler?p=1100753#post1100753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another cheesy way would be the Immunity merit out of Guide to the Traditions.<br /> If you invest 10+ points you are nigh impossible to kill.<br /> Recommended to take precautions against horrible mind shattering things the NC could do to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is WORSE. A Nexus Crawler isn't logical or smart, it doesn't have tactics. It gets bored easily. After killing a few PCs and NPCs it will wander off and find something more interesting (in its warped &quot;mind&quot; this could mean anything).<br /> <br /> But give it something it CAN'T kill? For me that sets it a challenge. This is entirely novel for a NC, something it can't warp to the point of death is just... perverse. Expect to be warped into something so horrible that you may as well be dead (and you'll certainly wish you were).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}